    "result_text": "The full build is green. Here's what I implemented.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required that owner responses carry a `bulkSignupWarning` flag \u2014 `true` once **more than 80** owners have already been registered for the current business day, otherwise `false`. The acceptance test reads it back via `GET /api/owners/{id}` and asserts `false` on a fresh create.\n\nFollowing the codebase's established pattern (derived owner fields are declared as `readOnly` properties in the OpenAPI schema and surfaced on the generated `OwnerDto`), I made two changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `bulkSignupWarning` readOnly boolean property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**\n   - Added a `BULK_SIGNUP_WARNING_THRESHOLD = 80` constant.\n   - Extracted the daily-count logic into a shared `countOwnersRegisteredOn(LocalDate)` helper (the daily-limit rule now reuses it), since the warning accumulates over the same per-business-day bucket \u2014 exactly what the test comment describes.\n   - Added `applyBulkSignupWarning(OwnerDto)`, which sets the flag to `count > 80` for the current business day (`toBusinessDay(LocalDate.now())`, consistent with how new registrations are dated).\n   - Called it on both the `getOwner` and `addOwner` response DTOs.\n\nUnmapped-target handling: MapStruct isn't configured to error on unmapped targets, so adding the field (which has no source on the `Owner` entity) is safe \u2014 the controller populates it explicitly.\n\n`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` and `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
