    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is structurally clean and idiomatic for this controller:\n\n- **Right unit / no duplication:** The counting logic that previously lived inline in `rejectDailyLimitReached` is extracted into `countOwnersRegisteredOn(...)` and then reused by both the daily-limit check and the new warning. That removes the duplication the second feature would otherwise have introduced, rather than copy-pasting the stream.\n- **Consistent with surroundings:** The new private helpers (`countOwnersRegisteredOn`, `applyBulkSignupWarning`) follow the established pattern in this class \u2014 small, focused, well-documented private methods alongside `rejectDailyLimitReached` and `toBusinessDay`, all reaching through `clinicService` the same way. A maintainer here would find this natural. (One could argue the volume/business-day logic belongs in the service layer, but the existing daily-limit code already counts owners in the controller, so moving only this piece down would break local consistency \u2014 keeping it here is the more coherent choice.)\n- **No catch-all growth:** Two cohesive helpers plus a documented threshold constant mirroring the existing `DAILY_OWNER_LIMIT` constant; nothing is being overloaded.\n- **Additive:** GET and POST both route through the single `applyBulkSignupWarning` mutator, and the OpenAPI schema addition mirrors the field's `readOnly` siblings.\n\nNo structural changes needed.",
